---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_EMAIL } from '../../../consts';

const lastUpdated = 'October 29, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — EchoChess"
	description="Privacy policy for EchoChess, an offline chess sparring studio for iPhone. The app collects nothing: no accounts, no analytics, no tracking, no network requests."
>
	<section style="padding-top: 4rem;">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="privacy-content">
				<a href="/projects/echochess" class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to EchoChess</a>
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="app-name">for <strong>EchoChess</strong></p>
				<p class="last-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

				<div class="highlight-box">
					<p>
						EchoChess collects nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking,
						and no network request of any kind. Everything the app knows stays on your iPhone, and
						uninstalling the app removes all of it.
					</p>
				</div>

				<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
				<p>
					None. EchoChess does not ask for your name, email address, phone number, date of birth, location,
					or any other personal information, and it has no mechanism to receive it.
				</p>

				<h2>2. What Is Stored On Your Device</h2>
				<p>
					EchoChess keeps your training history locally on your device so the app can show you how far you
					have come. That record contains:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Which Scenarios you have completed, and the Ghost Mode each was completed in</li>
					<li>The star rating recorded for each completed Scenario</li>
					<li>How many Pulses and Rewinds you used during a Sparring Session</li>
					<li>Your Ghost Mode and display preferences</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					This record is written to a local database on your device. It is never uploaded, never sent to a
					server of ours, and never shared with anyone. Deleting the app deletes it permanently.
				</p>

				<h2>3. Network Activity</h2>
				<p>
					EchoChess makes no network requests. The chess engine that evaluates your moves runs on your
					device, the Scenario Deck ships inside the app, and the Daily Endgame is chosen from that same
					bundled content. The app behaves identically in airplane mode.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Third Parties</h2>
				<p>
					EchoChess contains no advertising SDK, no analytics SDK, no crash-reporting SDK, no social login,
					and no third-party service that receives data about you.
				</p>
				<p>
					Apple may collect diagnostic information — such as crash reports — according to your device
					settings. That collection is performed by Apple, governed by
					<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>,
					and is not something EchoChess participates in or can read.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Permissions</h2>
				<p>
					EchoChess does not request access to your photos, contacts, calendars, location, microphone,
					camera, or health data. Haptic feedback and spoken move notation are produced by iOS on your
					device and require neither permission nor network.
				</p>

				<h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
				<p>
					EchoChess is suitable for general audiences and is not directed at children under 13. Because the
					app collects no personal information from anyone, it collects none from children.
				</p>

				<h2>7. Your Choices</h2>
				<p>
					You are in full control of the only data that exists — the training record on your device. You can
				clear a Scenario's progress from within the app, delete the app to remove everything permanently, or
				 turn off haptics and spoken notation in the app or in iOS Settings.
				</p>
				<p>
					Because we never receive your data, there is nothing for us to export, correct, or delete on your
					behalf.
				</p>

				<h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>
					If a future version of EchoChess ever changes what it stores or transmits, this page will say so
					before that version ships, and the date at the top will change. Continuing to use the app after a
					change means you accept the updated policy.
				</p>

				<h2>9. Contact</h2>
				<p>
					Questions about this policy, or about privacy in EchoChess, can go to
					<a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.privacy-content {
		max-width: 680px;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}
	h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
	.app-name { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
	.last-updated {
		font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	h2 { margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
	p { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
	ul {
		list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
	a { color: var(--accent); }
	.highlight-box {
		background: var(--surface-2, rgba(255,255,255,0.05));
		border: 1px solid var(--border, rgba(255,255,255,0.1));
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	.highlight-box p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}
</style>
